# User Ask Lines Are Edge To Edge

Once the member has sent a chat, **that ask in the transcript** has a
background that runs **chat-module edge to edge**. The fill is a lighter
shade of the member's own text color — brand blue in light, the
brightened member ink in dark.

This is the **sent line**, not the composer. The typing rail stays the
inset pill it already is. The rest of the transcript does not change:
same gutter, same type, same assistant lines, same ask copy sitting on
the same pixels. Only the wash behind the member's line reaches the
module edges.

This is app-wide and permanent.

## What this means on the surface

- Send an ask → the line lands in the thread with a full-width tint
  behind it, from one side of the chat module to the other.
- The avatar, the copy, and the timestamp stay on the shared gutter.
  They do not shift, re-wrap, or grow.
- Assistant answers have no matching band. Database-switch notes are
  not asks and stay bare.
- The composer at the bottom does not become a full-bleed bar. Do not
  "make the input edge to edge" to satisfy this rule.

## How it is wired

Shared CSS in `pages/wise.css` on `.sc-line-you:not(.sc-line-event)`.
A `::before` cancels the transcript inset with the same cqi formula
the output rails use, so a percentage cannot re-resolve against the
line. Isolation keeps the wash under the type.

## Rules for the agent

- Never restyle the composer to match this wash.
- Never move the ask's type, avatar, or gutter to "make the background
  full width." The fill bleeds; the line stays.
- Do not paint assistant lines, event rows, or the whole transcript.
- Do not fork this per page. A new chat host inherits it from the
  shared line — see the nothing-page-local rule.
